        "original_id": "3bc82659-acc1-5139-8990-c6827436e6f8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Southwest Florida International Airport, Henry E. Rohlsen Airport, Gateway, Florida, South Fort Myers, Lee County, Florida, Christiansted, St. Croix, United States Virgin Islands, Frederiksted\n- Companies: Hess Corporation\n- Systems: U.S. Virgin Islands Highway 66\n\nFacts:\n- Southwest Florida International Airport is a county-owned airport in the South Fort Myers region of unincorporated Lee County, Florida.\n- Gateway, Florida, is located just north of Southwest Florida International Airport.\n- Henry E. Rohlsen Airport is a public airport located six miles southwest of Christiansted on the island of St. Croix in the United States Virgin Islands.\n- U.S. Virgin Islands Highway 66 is an important intermediate link between the southern coast of St. Croix, including a Hess Corporation oil refinery and Henry E. Rohlsen International Airport, and the towns of Christiansted and Frederiksted.",
